    <h3>Find and Understand a 404 Error</h3>
    <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Understand what visitors see when
      they open a URL that does not exist.</p>
    <p>
      A 404 error means that the requested page cannot be found.
      A generic error page may not explain what happened or
      provide an easy way to return to the website.
    </p>
    <p>
      A better user experience would explain that the page is
      missing in a friendly way and provide a link back to the
      homepage.
    </p>
    <div class="links">
      <a href="https://ps8023724-sys.github.io/webpro-w10/this-page-does-not-exist.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Test missing URL ↗</a>
